<div class="qul-docs">
  <div>
    <h3>Export formats</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Juz data is exported in both <strong>JSON</strong> and <strong>SQLite</strong> formats.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3>JSON format</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">Here is an example of the JSON structure for the first juz:</p>
    <pre>
{
  "1": {
    "juz_number": 1,
    "verses_count": 148,
    "first_verse_key": "1:1",
    "last_verse_key": "2:141",
    "verse_mapping": {
      "1": "1-7",
      "2": "1-141"
    }
  }
}
    </pre>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto bg-gray-50 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200 mt-4">
      <table>
        <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Field</th>
          <th>Type</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>juz_number</code></td>
          <td>INTEGER</td>
          <td>The juz number (1 to 30).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>verses_count</code></td>
          <td>INTEGER</td>
          <td>Total number of verses in the juz.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>first_verse_key</code></td>
          <td>TEXT</td>
          <td>The key of the first verse in the juz (e.g. <code>1:1</code>).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>last_verse_key</code></td>
          <td>TEXT</td>
          <td>The key of the last verse in the juz (e.g. <code>2:141</code>).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>verse_mapping</code></td>
          <td>OBJECT</td>
          <td>
            A mapping of surah numbers to ayah ranges within this juz.
            For example, <code>"2": "1-141"</code> means Surah 2 contributes ayahs 1 to 141 to this juz.
          </td>
        </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
